-- title:
--   Deuring lifting for an endomorphism with order maximal at p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose residue field $\kappa_A =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A` has characteristic $p$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa_A$ which is elliptic. Let $\alpha_0$ be an additive endomorphism of the group of affine points $W(\kappa_A)$ belonging to [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28), i.e. either $\alpha_0 = 0$ or there are bivariate polynomials $n_X, d_X, n_Y, d_Y$ over $\kappa_A$ and a finite set $B$ of abscissae such that for every nonsingular affine point $(x,y)$ with $x \notin B$ the denominators do not vanish and $\alpha_0(x,y) = (n_X/d_X,\, n_Y/d_Y)(x,y)$. Let $t, q \in \mathbb Z$ satisfy $\alpha_0 \circ \alpha_0 + q\cdot\mathrm{id} = t\,\alpha_0$, assume $m^2 - tm + q \neq 0$ for every $m \in \mathbb Z$, and assume that for every $k_0 \in \mathbb Z$ with $p \mid t - 2k_0$ one has $p^2 \nmid k_0^2 - tk_0 + q$. Then there are a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $A$ whose reduction $E \bmod \mathfrak m_A$ has nonzero discriminant, a variable change $v$ over $\kappa_A$ with $v \cdot (E \bmod \mathfrak m_A) = W$, and an element $\alpha$ of [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) for the base change $E_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ to itself, such that for every affine point $P$ of $E_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ the reduction map [`WeierstrassCurve.reduceHom`](def/WeierstrassCurve_ReduceHom.html#L481) (which sends a point with integral abscissa to the point with residue coordinates, and all other affine points and the point at infinity to $0$), followed by the identification of $(E \bmod \mathfrak m_A)(\kappa_A)$ with $W(\kappa_A)$ supplied by $v$, carries $\alpha P$ to $\alpha_0$ of the image of $P$.
--
--   This is Deuring's lifting theorem in the case where the quadratic order $\mathbb Z[X]/(X^2-tX+q)$ generated by the given endomorphism is maximal at $p$, with the lift produced at a prescribed place $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above $p$ and with the special fibre recovered only up to a Weierstrass variable change. It is used to obtain the statement for an arbitrary geometric endomorphism, [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_mem_rationalHomSet`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_mem_rationalHomSet).
